{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790248225,"nonce":"Bd7VdcGTjKoxQU2JQKuQS/gkFD8=","message":"Portable capability negotiation is now implemented locally on top of the typed Future work.\n\n- GPUFeatureName and every GPUSupportedLimits attribute are generated from the vendored IDL as gpu.Feature and gpu.Limit.\n- GpuAdapter and GpuDevice expose supports(Feature) and limit(Limit).\n- GpuDeviceDescriptor accumulates required feature and limit entries without dynamic maps; requestDeviceWith() passes them into wgpu DeviceDescriptor and returns Future\u003cGpuDevice\u003e.\n- Requests below WebGPU defaults are clamped to the defaults. Invalid values, unsupported wgpu 30 draft features/limits, and backend capability failures reject the Future.\n- caribou-bindgen now supports finite catalogs sourced from readonly interface attributes.\n- The Haxe GPU fixture exercises limit queries and configured device creation.\n\nChecks pass for bindgen, GPU unit/catalog tests, the workspace, fixture compilation, and wasm32-unknown-unknown. The runtime fixture reaches adapter acquisition but this host still reports no suitable Metal adapter.","files":null}]}